{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The AITER FP16 path is not applicable here (its 16-bit GEMM backend requires BF16/FP32 output), so I’m moving to a focused Triton implementation for `M≤256` while retaining the proven vendor GEMM for the four large workloads. The custom path reads `B` directly in its existing `[N,K]` layout and avoids any preprocessing."}}
