{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"The official run exposed a timing detail the event-only tuner hid: AITER’s decorated Python wrapper adds roughly 50–70 µs of host overhead, wiping out the small-shape kernel win. The large kernels still improve, but I’m bypassing that wrapper and calling the already-loaded hipBLASLt extension directly; this should retain the tuned algorithm without the Python dispatch tax."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 python - <<'PY'\nimport torch,time,statistics,importlib,aiter\nM,N,K=16,28672,4096\nA=torch.randn((M,K),device='cuda',dtype=torch.float16);B=torch.randn((N,K),device='cuda',dtype=torch.float16)\naiter.hipb_create_extension()\nmod=importlib.import_module('aiter.jit.module_hipbsolgemm')\nsol=477461\nfuncs=[('torch',lambda:A@B.T),('wrapper',lambda:aiter.hipb_mm(A,B.T,sol)),('direct',lambda:mod.hipb_mm(A,B.T,sol))]\nfor name,fn in funcs:\n for _ in range(10):fn()\n torch.cuda.synchronize()\n vals=[]\n for _ in range(100):\n  torch.cuda.synchronize();t=time.perf_counter_ns();fn();torch.cuda.synchronize();vals.append((time.perf_counter_ns()-t)/1e6)\n print(name,'wall median',statistics.median(vals),'min',min(vals),'mean',statistics.mean(vals))\n s=torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True);e=torch.cuda.Event(enable_timing=True);s.record()\n for _ in range(100):fn()\n e.record();e.synchronize();print(name,'event',s.elapsed_time(e)/100)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
