{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"Cold-cache measurements explain the discrepancy exactly: the verifier evicts the 224 MiB weight, while repeated local calls let it reside in the MI355X cache. Under cold weights, PyTorch is decisively best through `M=256`; the tuned algorithms remain genuinely faster only at `M=972`, `2053`, and `2379`. I’m narrowing the dispatch to those three cases and using the direct extension entry point."}}
